{"id":"wikibooks:peach-cobbler","verdict":"keep","countries":["US"],"reason":"Peach cobbler is an American dessert","recipes":[{"source":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook%3APeach_Cobbler","status":"fixed","reason":"Decode leftover HTML fraction entities","ingredients":["1 cup all-purpose flour","½ cup butter","¼ cup milk","2 cans (15 oz / 425 g) peaches","½ cup white granulated sugar"],"steps":["Combine flour, butter, and milk. Cut together to make dough and set aside.","Pour peaches in 9x13-inch baking pan. Sprinkle sugar on top.","Roll out crust and place on top of peaches.","Bake at 350 °F or until top is browned lightly (approximately one hour)."]}]}
